# Plan Mode: Front-End Advanced Template

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides an advanced planning template for complex front-end features in the PolygonExpress project. It is designed for planning sophisticated components with complex state management, API integrations, and cross-component interactions.

This file complements:
- **front-end-workflow-reference.md**: Core front-end development workflow
- **plan-mode-front-end-basic.md**: Basic planning template
- **dev-mode-log-based.md**: Implementation approach

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/plan-mode-advanced.mdc
```

## Advanced Template Structure

When this template is applied, the planning folder will be structured as follows:

```
planning/
  ├── requirements.md (Detailed requirements)
  ├── context-component.md (Component analysis)
  ├── context-state-flow.md (State management flow)
  ├── context-api-integration.md (API integration details)
  ├── implementation-component.md (Implementation approach)
  ├── implementation-state-management.md (State implementation details)
  ├── implementation-api-integration.md (API implementation details)
  ├── test-cheatsheet.md (Comprehensive testing scenarios)
  └── README.md (Overview)
```

